  "implemented": [
    "Core-only typed start/cancel command component consumes trusted Binding/Run/epoch/call identity separately from strict model arguments; no new model/CLI/IPC entry is activated",
    "Command identity is derived from operation, Binding ID/generation, source Run/epoch and call, never task arguments. Only the new delegation commands opt into exact canonical envelope digest replay in the existing event_log receipt columns",
    "Private payload hashes the credential; neither its raw value nor duplicate task content is persisted. Changed arguments, credential or compatibility digest conflict with an existing exact receipt",
    "Recovery derives immutable Run/Conversation owner scope and checks the sole recorded receipt before current admission, directory observation, Registry or factory; new work still requires actual current attested identity, member, frozen policy and control",
    "Start consumes a matching prepared proof and exact full task/runtime/original directory, revalidates the current snapshot, uses the production child factory and original external-directory permission flow, and commits graph/event/receipt atomically",
    "Start business refusal rolls back a savepoint before recording a stable failed TaskReport. Storage faults abort the entire command rather than recording false business rejection",
    "Model cancel requires current exact parent authority but survives current global disable/depth tightening; only direct children are visible, unknown/foreign tasks return only requested task_id and unknown",
    "Model cancellation uses the original causal-tree Run settlement and after-commit pump, preserves separately User-taken-over branches, treats terminal/taken-over root as no-op, and never reruns effects on receipt replay",
    "Current-attempt TaskReport reads the exact persisted final Run message with ownership and takeover sequence fence, caps UTF-8 result to256KiB including ellipsis, returns original result_ref, exposes pending permission ID without raw directory/tool details, and reflects cleanup only for canceled status"
  ],
